{
  "summary": "Revision 2026-10-02 (crowd after submission, design §20, reports 📓️crowd-plots-report.md and 📓️crowd-distributions-core-report.md): by default the others' answers show only once the learner has submitted — on the results always, on a quiz's page once a run of that quiz is submitted, in a run only when the learner asks ('Show it now' / 'Hide it again'; ephemeral QuizState.asked, events crowd-asked / crowd-unasked, ends with the run); the persisted preference others (never | submitted | always) replaces showAnswers; crowdGate decides per place. Everything about the others is a figure: per task a table of small columns (rows = items, columns = categories, places or values; the share on the cap, the learner's own answer in the active colour with ●, the correct one with ✓ on results, a presence-coloured dot per learner thinking it now) and histograms of the scores of all runs (run, task, matching dimension) with the learner's own bin; new modules 📊️plot and a rewritten 🗳️crowd; the crowd lines under the items and the 'Everyone' column are gone. CrowdView carries the distributions: scores (ten bins) on the view and on every crowd task and places on sorting items, with scoreBin, placeBin and presented in both cores, numpy/Counter-corroborated vectors, the proctor tally keeping score bins and orders (PROJECTOR_REVISION 5). Verified: quiz react 613 tests and typecheck, quiz TS 297, quiz Rust 107, proctor 87 + 15 + 17, parity 108/108, taxonomy clean, end-to-end specs shared-presence and phone on a throw-away stack, screenshots from a private stack with the new proctor (crowd_plots_shots.ts). Not run: the end-to-end projects boot, desktop, shortage, pets and the rehearsal topology, blocked by other sessions' edits in flight (see the report).",
